                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\colon X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers+object"} real numbers object
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+real+numbers"} Dedekind real numbers
          %h2#foundational_status Foundational status
          %h3#in_set_theory_2 In set theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            has a tight apartness relation. In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations+of+mathematics"} foundations of mathematics
            which states that every set has a tight apartness relation.
          %p
            %strong> Axiom of tight apartness
            \: Every set has a tight apartness relation.
          %p
            Alternatively, one could take the tight apartness relaiton to be foundational, in which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+extensionality"} axiom of extensionality
            becomes
          %p
            %strong>
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+extensionality"} Axiom of extensionality
            \: for any set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
